# Project Tech Stack & Libraries

## 🐍 Backend (Python / Django)
These libraries power the "Brain", "Ears", and "Voice" of the Tutor.

| Library Name | Use Case in "Vaathiyar" | Why we chose it |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **`django`** | **Core Framework**. Manages the overall application, database, and admin panel. | Best-in-class security and structure. |
| **`channels`** | **Real-time Comms**. Enables WebSockets support in Django. | Essential for streaming Chat & Audio instantly. |
| **`daphne`** | **ASGI Server**. Runs Django in Asynchronous mode. | Required by `channels` to handle simultaneous connections. |
| **`requests`** | **API Client**. Sends HTTP POST requests to [Ollama](file:///d:/final%20year%20project/V/backend/llm_engine/domain_local/ollama_provider.py#8-44). | Simple, standard way to talk to local APIs. |
| **`google-genai`** | **Cloud AI**. SDK for Google Gemini 2.0 Flash. | Allows fallback to a smarter cloud model if needed. |
| **`chromadb`** | **Vector Database**. Stores "Knowledge" (textbook chunks) as vectors. | Runs locally (no server setup), very fast for RAG. |
| **`langchain`** | **RAG Framework**. Orchestrates PDF reading, splitting, and AI logic. | Industry standard logic for connecting Data to AI. |
| **`langchain-text-splitters`**| **Text Processing**. Splits large PDFs into small readable paragraphs. | Helps the AI "digest" big books. |
| **`sentence-transformers`**| **Embeddings**. Converts text into math (vectors) for search. | Fast, runs on CPU, accurate for English. |
| **`pypdf`** | **PDF Parser**. Extracts raw text from [.pdf](file:///d:/final%20year%20project/V/Grokking%20Algorithms%20-%20An%20illustrated%20guide%20for%20programmers%20and%20other%20curious%20people-8.pdf) files. | Reliable PDF reading. |
| **`edge-tts`** | **Voice Output**. Generates MP3 speech from text. | Uses Microsoft Neural Voices (High Quality) for free. |
| **`librosa`** | **Audio Analysis**. Loads raw WAV files to detect properties. | Standard tool for audio/music signal processing. |
| **`numpy`** | **Math**. Handling array operations for Audio/AI data. | The foundation of all Python AI. |

---

## ⚛️ Frontend (TypeScript / Next.js)
These libraries power the interactive Dashboard, Canvas, and Code Editor.

| Library Name | Use Case in "Vaathiyar" | Why we chose it |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **`next.js`** | **UI Framework**. The main React application structure. | Fast, SEO-friendly, easy file-based routing. |
| **`react-use-websocket`** | **Live Connection**. Manages the WS link to Backend. | Handles auto-reconnection and message queuing robustly. |
| **`react-konva`** | **Whiteboard**. Renders the infinite drawing canvas. | High-performance wrapper for HTML5 Canvas. |
| **`monaco-editor`** | **Code Editor**. The text editor component. | It IS the VS Code editor, embedded (Great DX). |
| **`pyodide`** | **Code Execution**. Runs Python code in the browser. | Secure (Sandboxed) and doesn't crash the server. |
| **`lucide-react`** | **Icons**. The icons you see (Mic, Send, Terminal). | Clean, consistent, lightweight SVG icons. |
| **`framer-motion`** | **Animations**. Smooth sidebar slides and fades. | The best animation library for React. |
| **`tailwind-css`** | **Styling**. Colors, spacing, dark mode. | Standard for modern, responsive web design. |
